# Makes the repository citable. GitHub reads this file and offers
# "Cite this repository"; Zenodo picks up the metadata when archiving.
# TODO: fill in name, ORCID and affiliation.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "lvgrid-rl: a training environment for RL agents controlling low-voltage grids"
abstract: >-
  Modular training and evaluation environment for reinforcement learning agents
  that autonomously resolve EN 50160 voltage band violations as well as line and
  transformer overloads in low-voltage distribution grids, by curtailing PV
  infeed, shifting heat pump and charging loads, and controlling battery
  storage. Grid simulation with pandapower and SimBench, agents with
  Stable-Baselines3.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtroeschel/lvgrid-rl"
